&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;p-rich_text_section&quot;&gt;And we&#39;re building all of that on the intelligence of a single AI engine —&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong data-stringify-type=&quot;bold&quot;&gt;Loomi &lt;/strong&gt;— so that personalization isn&#39;t only autonomous…it&#39;s also consistent.From retail to financial services, hospitality to gaming, businesses use Bloomreach to drive higher growth and lasting loyalty. We power personalization for more than 1,400 global brands, including American Eagle, Sonepar, and Pandora.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Revenue Operations Analyst - 12 Month Maternity Cover&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Bloomreach has best-in-class customer and product data, and as our Revenue Operations team continues to evolve, we are looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Revenue Operations Analyst&lt;/strong&gt; to support and help scale our next phase of growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this high-impact role, you will partner closely with the Revenue Operations team and EMEA Sales stakeholders to deliver accurate reporting, actionable insights, and operational support. You will work across multiple data sources to help drive visibility into performance, improve processes, and enable data-driven decision making across the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support data analysis across multiple systems to help inform decision-making for Bloomreach’s Sales teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist Revenue Operations leaders in partnering with EMEA Sales stakeholders to track performance against key targets&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and improve dashboards and reports to ensure timely and accurate visibility into business metrics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver recurring reporting and insights to cross-functional stakeholders (Sales, Marketing, Customer Success, Finance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the execution of Revenue Operations initiatives and projects, ensuring high-quality and timely delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify data inconsistencies or process gaps and proactively suggest improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to ad hoc analysis and special projects as needed&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2–4 years of experience in data analysis, sales operations, revenue operations, or similar roles&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong working knowledge of Microsoft Excel, Google Sheets, and data visualization/reporting tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CRM systems (e.g. Salesforce) and familiarity with tools like Clari is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analytical mindset with the ability to interpret data and translate it into clear insights&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail and ability to manage multiple priorities effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Good communication skills, with the ability to present findings clearly to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive and curious, with a desire to learn and improve processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work in a fast-paced, technology-driven environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BA/BS degree or equivalent experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
